---
source: tests/cli_root.rs
expression: out
---
qam – capture frames/clips and motion from RTSP/ONVIF cameras.

Common commands:
  snap     grab a frame (positional camera name allowed)
  clip     short clip; drop audio with --no-audio
  audio    record audio clip (default 10s, copy codec, .wav)
  doctor   checks media engine, reachability, optional RTSP probe

Usage: qam [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  add         Add or update a camera
  list        List saved cameras [alias: ls]
  snap        Capture a single frame to a file
  clip        Record a short clip to a file
  audio       Record an audio-only clip to a file [alias: record-audio]
  discover    Discover cameras on the local network via ONVIF WS-Discovery
  watch       Run motion detection and execute an action
  doctor      Run basic checks (media engine, config present, camera ports reachable)
  slack       Manage Slack configuration
  version     Show qam version
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for qam for the specified shell
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --version
          version for qam

      --config <path>
          Path to config file (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/camsnap/config.yaml)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  qam add --name kitchen --host 192.168.0.175 --user tapo --pass secret --rtsp-transport udp
  --stream stream2
  qam snap kitchen --out shot.jpg
  qam snap kitchen --slack-channel #security --slack-message "Kitchen check!"
  qam clip kitchen --dur 5s --no-audio --out clip.mp4
  qam clip kitchen --dur 10s --slack-channel @steve
  qam audio kitchen --seconds 10 --out audio.wav
  qam watch kitchen --threshold 0.2 --cooldown 5s --action 'qam snap kitchen --slack-channel
  #alerts'
  qam doctor --probe --rtsp-transport udp
